{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>וינחם.</b> Far be it that HaShem should relent. The Torah only speaks in the language of human beings, like \"ויעל\" (Genesis 35:13), \"וירד\" (ibid. 11:5), \"ישמח ד׳ במעשיו\" (Psalms 104:31), \"ויתעצב אל לבו\" (Genesis 6:6). And behold, Samuel said: \"and also the Eternal One of Israel will not lie and will not relent\" (I Samuel 15:29), and there it is written \"נחמתי\". Some interpret it in the sense of a council, and there is no need."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :register {:flags {0 ["the Eternal"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:45.083596148Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}